--- !u!114 &205473522803644395
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6033785374627301050}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ac3fc7ab0c1d424ca4328b935a45df1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  masterCanvasGroup: {fileID: 4779224392998917178}
  choiceCanvasGroup: {fileID: 4982395088408367858}
  endingCanvasGroup: {fileID: 4715600169002021750}
  epilogueCanvasGroup: {fileID: 6082690514454041098}
  fadeOverlay: {fileID: 8667066879853006167}
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 6782632711719685234}
  returnEndingBackgroundImage: {fileID: 1810673049472658662}
  destroyEndingBackgroundImage: {fileID: 8659142440880499552}
  arrivalText: {fileID: 4757369688021603193}
  choicePromptText: {fileID: 3130122012155969931}
  returnButton: {fileID: 4612324043002941455}
  returnButtonLabel: {fileID: 7389374472446829102}
  returnButtonSub: {fileID: 5051322930531897111}
  destroyButton: {fileID: 2700929467537972305}
  destroyButtonLabel: {fileID: 4092214065119295625}
  destroyButtonSub: {fileID: 7335049590469428508}
  endingTitleText: {fileID: 9085056406395494415}
  endingBodyText: {fileID: 5416272624726233516}
  epilogueText: {fileID: 5150863709560782949}
  toMainMenuButton: {fileID: 6241919395489602742}
  toMainMenuLabel: {fileID: 9213698812262619821}
  mainMenuButtonGroup: {fileID: 7101904951450542569}
  initialBlackHold: 1
  screenFadeInTime: 2
  arrivalFadeInTime: 1.4
  choiceFadeInTime: 1
  choiceHoldAfterType: 0.8
  endingTransitionTime: 1.6
  endingFadeInTime: 1.2
  epilogueFadeInTime: 1
  typewriterSpeed: 0.022
  pauseAtParagraph: 0.35
  returnEndingTint: {r: 0.85, g: 0.72, b: 0.3, a: 1}
  destroyEndingTint: {r: 0, g: 1, b: 0.87058824, a: 1}
  arrivalNarration: "The chamber is silent.\n\nAt the heart of the Sacred Grounds,
    where every corrupted knight once knelt and every rift in the sky traces its
    origin \u2014 it stands.\n\nThe Monolith of the Sun.\n\nIts light does not blind.
    It waits. As if it has always been waiting for you."
  choicePrompt: 'The King''s order echoes in your mind.

    But the Monolith does
    not belong to any king.'
  returnButtonText: RETURN IT
  returnButtonSubText: Fulfil the King's decree.
  returnEndingTitle: "ENDING A  \xB7  THE CROWNED SUN"
  returnEndingBody: "You carry the Monolith back through the rifts, through the ruins,
    through the gates of a kingdom that never expected you to return.\n\nThe King
    weeps when he sees it. Then he stops weeping.\n\nWithin a season, the rifts close.
    The Sacred Grounds grow quiet. The Royal Army, empowered by the Monolith's light,
    marches beyond the old borders \u2014 into lands that never asked for a king.\n\nThe
    White Maiden is not seen again. Some say she vanished the morning the Monolith
    was placed on the throne-altar. Others say she was the first to kneel before
    it.\n\nYou are celebrated. Promoted. Given a name in the histories.\n\nAt night,
    through the palace window, you sometimes see the horizon glow gold \u2014 the
    same colour as the Monolith's light. You have stopped wondering whether that
    is a good thing."
  returnEpilogue: 'The rifts are closed. The kingdom is vast.

    Some lights cast
    very long shadows.'
  destroyButtonText: DESTROY IT
  destroyButtonSubText: Let no one wield this power.
  destroyEndingTitle: "ENDING B  \xB7  THE LAST LIGHT"
  destroyEndingBody: "Your weapon strikes the surface of the Monolith.\n\nFor a moment
    \u2014 nothing.\n\nThen the light inside it spreads outward, not in an explosion,
    but in something quieter. A breath releasing after centuries of being held.\n\nThe
    rifts seal themselves. Not slowly, not with ceremony \u2014 simply, finally,
    done. The Sacred Grounds shudder once and go still. The corruption recedes like
    a tide that has forgotten how to return.\n\nThe King receives no Monolith. He
    receives no soldier, either.\n\nYou remain in the Sacred Grounds long after the
    light fades. The White Maiden finds you there, sitting in the dust where the
    Monolith stood. She does not ask what you did. She already knows.\n\nShe sits
    beside you.\n\nOutside, for the first time in living memory, the sky is whole."
  destroyEpilogue: 'The Monolith is gone. The sky is unbroken.

    Some things are
    worth losing everything for.'
  mainMenuButtonText: Return to Main Menu
